    "## Q3 · Failure Modes &nbsp;&nbsp; \n",
    "\n",
    "For each failure mode: describe **(i) what it looks like in practice**, **(ii) the root cause**, and **(iii) one mitigation strategy**.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "bccfb557",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Q3(a) · Mode Collapse &nbsp; \n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a7dc52b6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Your Answer:**\n",
    "\n",
    "| | |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| **(i) What it looks like** | The generator produces very similar or identical images regardless of the input noise. |\n",
    "| **(ii) Root cause** | The generator discovers a few outputs that consistently fool the discriminator and keeps generating only those. |\n",
    "| **(iii) Mitigation** | Use techniques such as Minibatch Discrimination or Wasserstein GAN (WGAN) to encourage output diversity. |\n"
   ]
  },
